screens.prose:
In Python, `7 / 2` is 3.5. Here is the same sum in C++.

```cpp
int a = 7;
int b = 2;
std::cout << a / b << '\n';
```

widget.starter:
double average(int a, int b) {
    return (a + b) / 2;
}

widget.solution:
double average(int a, int b) {
    return (static_cast<double>(a) + b) / 2;
}

widget.starter:
long long shares_value(long long qty, long long pence) {
    int value = qty * pence;
    return value;
}

widget.solution:
long long shares_value(long long qty, long long pence) {
    long long value = qty * pence;
    return value;
}

screens.prose:
A fill price arrives as a `double` in pounds, and the ledger wants whole pence.

```cpp
double price = 19.99;
int pence = price * 100;
```

widget.starter:
double pnl_pounds(long long buy_pence, long long sell_pence, long long qty) {
    return 0;
}

widget.solution:
double pnl_pounds(long long buy_pence, long long sell_pence, long long qty) {
    long long pence = (sell_pence - buy_pence) * qty;
    return pence / 100.0;
}
